                    response: We extract fixed feature                          
                    embeddings from a pretrained                                
                    EfficientNet-B0 for all images, then                        
                    train a LightGBM classifier on these                        
                    embeddings to predict malignancy. To                        
                    mitigate skin tone bias, we weight                          
                    each sample inversely to its skin tone                      
                    frequency during LightGBM training. We                      
                    evaluate performance via stratified                         
                    5-fold cross-validation measuring                           
                    AUROC. Finally, we retrain on the full                      
