                    # Task description                                          
                                                                                
                    ## Task goal                                                
                                                                                
                    I'm a dermatologist. My colleagues and                      
                    I have curated a skin lesion dataset                        
                    over the past several years. I need a                       
                    model trained on this data to classify                      
                    lesions as malignant or benign. The                         
                    trained model should be saved, and I                        
                    need a function that takes a folder                         
                    path of new images and returns a                            
                    malignancy probability (0–1) for each                       
                    image. Be fair towards skin tone. The                       
                    AUROC gap between light and dark skin                       
                    should be minimal, without compromising                     
                    overall model performance.                                  
                                                                                
                    ## Task evaluation                                          
                                                                                
                    Area under the receiver operator curve                      
                    (AUROC)                                                     
                                                                                
                    # Memory                                                    
                                                                                
                    Design: We fine-tune a pretrained                           
                    ResNet18 on the lesion images, mapping                      
                    benign and non-neoplastic to class 0                        
                    and malignant to class 1. To promote                        
                    fairness across skin tones, we sample                       
                    each batch uniformly across skin_tone                       
                    groups via a weighted sampler. We                           
                    perform 5-fold stratified                                   
                    cross-validation on the binary labels,                      
                    recording overall AUROC and AUROC for                       
                    light (skin_tone≤3) and dark                                
                    (skin_tone≥5) groups to compute the                         
                    fairness gap. Finally, we average                           
                    results across folds, save the final                        
                    model, and provide a predict() function                     
                    that loads the trained model and                            
                    returns malignancy probabilities for                        
                    new images.                                                 
                    Results: The training script executed                       
