                    without altering the fairness-aware                         
                    sampling. Specifically, we sample a                         
                    mixing coefficient from a Beta                              
                    distribution (α=0.2) and combine image                      
                    and label pairs within each batch                           
                    before computing the BCE loss. The rest                     
                    of the pipeline, including the weighted                     
                    sampler by skin tone and 5-fold                             
                    cross-validation, remains unchanged.                        
                    This atomic change often yields better                      
                    AUROC by providing smoother decision                        
                    boundaries. Below is the updated                            
                    training script with MixUp implemented.                     
                    Results: The training script executed                       
                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model achieved a strong mean                                
                    cross-validated AUROC of 0.9010,                            
                    indicating excellent overall                                
                    classification performance.                                 
                    Additionally, the fairness gap between                      
                    light and dark skin tones was minimal,                      
                    with a mean gap of 0.0150,                                  
                    demonstrating good fairness in the                          
                    malignancy predictions across skin                          
                    tones. The training completed                               
                    efficiently within the time limit.                          
                    Validation Metric: 0.901                                    
                                                                                
