                    evaluation ran successfully without any                     
                    errors. The model achieved a strong                         
                    mean cross-validation AUROC of 0.9040,                      
                    indicating good overall performance in                      
                    classifying malignant vs benign                             
                    lesions. The fairness gap between light                     
                    and dark skin tones is very low                             
                    (0.0117), demonstrating effective                           
                    mitigation of bias while maintaining                        
                    high accuracy. The training used MixUp                      
                    augmentation and 4-fold test-time                           
